(5625835, 814494, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> I like the crisp focus you achieved, but I''d like to see a bot more shallow depth of field.  I''d like to see the flower isolated from the rest of the scene with focus.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Great, natural lighting.  Everything was nicely and evenly lit with no lost details in harsh highlights or deep shadows.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> The composition isn''t bad, but it also doesn''t jump out at grab my eye''s attention.  The leaves of the plant that were left on the focal plane adds distractions to the eye.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Its not a bad photograph at all.  I think that the sub-5 scoring is a bit harsh, but flowers and voters are tough to figure out here.<br/> <br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b> <br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: I like the crisp focus you achieved, but I''d like to see a bot more shallow depth of field.  I''d like to see the flower isolated from the rest of the scene with focus. Lighting: Great, natural lighting.  Everything was nicely and evenly lit with no lost details in harsh highlights or deep shadows. Composition/Content: The composition isn''t bad, but it also doesn''t jump out at grab my eye''s attention.  The leaves of the plant that were left on the focal plane adds distractions to the eye. My Opinion: Its not a bad photograph at all.  I think that the sub-5 scoring is a bit harsh, but flowers and voters are tough to figure out here. Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,Eric ', '2009-08-27 03:16:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(5625838, 814319, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Interesting depth if field, and nice focus on the key portion of your subject.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> I like the tones captured here with the use of natural and available light.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> I think that the composition that you chose really hurt your score.  The small portion of the cow itself to the left of the frame adds a very large distraction.  Add to that, your subject is centered in the mirror, and the mirror is pretty much centered in the frame.  Definite composition flaws that lend to lower votes as a general rule.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Unfortunately, I think this one scored pretty close to its potential.  It was a comical take on the challenge, and your comments reflect that.<br/> <br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b> <br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Interesting depth if field, and nice focus on the key portion of your subject. Lighting: I like the tones captured here with the use of natural and available light. Composition/Content: I think that the composition that you chose really hurt your score.  The small portion of the cow itself to the left of the frame adds a very large distraction.  Add to that, your subject is centered in the mirror, and the mirror is pretty much centered in the frame.  Definite composition flaws that lend to lower votes as a general rule. My Opinion: Unfortunately, I think this one scored pretty close to its potential.  It was a comical take on the challenge, and your comments reflect that. Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,Eric ', '2009-08-27 03:22:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5625844, 813644, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First off, always try to include some info about the shot in the Photographer''s Comments section. It really helps out when we know what the photographer was thinking and what equipment/lighting/etc. were used, especially when you request a critique.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Your chosen depth of field is absolutely the main strength of the image.  I really like the transition from crisp focus to soft blur.  Well captured!<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> I also like the even lighting you achieved here.  No detail was lost in harsh highlights or in deep, dark shadows.  <br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> I would like to see a bit stronger composition here.  While I am no stickler for the ''rules of photography'' by any means, this one is just a bit too centered for my eye.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> 5.6 is a nice, strong score for this image.  Flowers are so hard to guess with the voters here.  To me, I don''t see the subject as pink.  It seems more purple.  Anyway, your excellent depth of field pulled a nice score.<br/> <br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b> <br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  First off, always try to include some info about the shot in the Photographer''s Comments section. It really helps out when we know what the photographer was thinking and what equipment/lighting/etc. were used, especially when you request a critique. Camera Work/Technical: Your chosen depth of field is absolutely the main strength of the image.  I really like the transition from crisp focus to soft blur.  Well captured! Lighting: I also like the even lighting you achieved here.  No detail was lost in harsh highlights or in deep, dark shadows.   Composition/Content: I would like to see a bit stronger composition here.  While I am no stickler for the ''rules of photography'' by any means, this one is just a bit too centered for my eye. My Opinion: 5.6 is a nice, strong score for this image.  Flowers are so hard to guess with the voters here.  To me, I don''t see the subject as pink.  It seems more purple.  Anyway, your excellent depth of field pulled a nice score. Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,Eric ', '2009-08-27 03:27:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(5625907, 814194, 82707, '<td valign="top">Congrats Roz!  Great work!</td>', 'Congrats Roz!  Great work!', '2009-08-27 05:06:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5625930, 814937, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Awesome.  I love the detail of the petals that fade into a very interesting, blurred background.  The colors of the flower play very well against the browns and greens in the background.  Well seen and well executed.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Flawless.  Whites on flowers are difficult to expose right.  Nice work, especially considering the detail in the browns that you still captured.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Wonderful composition, and I really like the flower that you chose to submit. I like the fact that there is a great deal of beauty left in the flower, but there are also signs of death and dying creeping in.  Whether or not you meant to capture a statement, you did.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> The voters absolutely missed this one.  While I have not been through all the entries in this challenge, this has been my favorite flower capture of the challenge thus far.  It is surely much better, in my opinion, than many that scored higher.<br/> <br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b> <br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Awesome.  I love the detail of the petals that fade into a very interesting, blurred background.  The colors of the flower play very well against the browns and greens in the background.  Well seen and well executed. Lighting: Flawless.  Whites on flowers are difficult to expose right.  Nice work, especially considering the detail in the browns that you still captured. Composition/Content: Wonderful composition, and I really like the flower that you chose to submit. I like the fact that there is a great deal of beauty left in the flower, but there are also signs of death and dying creeping in.  Whether or not you meant to capture a statement, you did. My Opinion: The voters absolutely missed this one.  While I have not been through all the entries in this challenge, this has been my favorite flower capture of the challenge thus far.  It is surely much better, in my opinion, than many that scored higher. Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,Eric ', '2009-08-27 05:33:49.000000', NULL, 0),
